<MakerLayout title="How to Print Browser-Made Worksheets Cleanly — PARADOX Makers" description="A practical guide to printing browser-generated puzzles, cards, tickets and charts as clean PDFs or paper handouts."><main class="maker-main"><article class="maker-why"><div class="maker-label">GUIDE · PRINTING</div><h1>How to print browser-made worksheets cleanly</h1><p>Browser generators are convenient because they work instantly and do not need a document upload service. Printing is the final step, and a few settings make the difference between a clean worksheet and a cramped page.</p><h2>Preview before printing</h2><p>Always use the print preview. Check whether the generated grid, ticket sheet or certificate fits inside the printable area. If the browser adds headers and footers, turn them off for a cleaner result.</p><h2>Use Save as PDF when sending files</h2><p>If someone needs the generated result electronically, choose Save as PDF instead of taking a screenshot. The resulting PDF keeps text and lines sharper and is easier to print later.</p><h2>Use the right orientation</h2><p>Dense tables often benefit from landscape orientation. Certificates and portrait worksheets usually work better in portrait. The preview is the fastest way to decide.</p><h2>Do not overfill the page</h2><p>More content is not always better. A slightly shorter list with generous spacing usually creates a more readable printed worksheet than a maximum-density page.</p><h2>Keep the original inputs</h2><p>Save your source list separately when the activity matters. That lets you generate a new version later without rebuilding the content from memory.</p><p><a href="/#tools">Explore the generators →</a></p></article></main></MakerLayout>
